#: ../../talk/call.rst:3
msgid "Joining a call"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:6
msgid "Starting or joining a call"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:9
msgid "Browser and Talk Desktop client"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:11
msgid "When you are part of a conversation and have permission to do so, you can start a call at any time by clicking ``Start call`` in the top bar. When a call is already in progress, join it by clicking the green ``Join call`` button in the chat area or the top bar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:14
msgid "Talk conversation with a green Join call button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:18
msgid "If you have not yet given permission to the browser or the Talk Desktop client to use your microphone and camera, you will be prompted to do so when you click ``Start call`` or ``Join call``. Choose the microphone and camera you would like to use and click ``Allow`` to grant access to your devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:22
msgid "You will see ``Media settings``, where you can customise your call experience:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:24
msgid "Talk media settings dialog before joining a call"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:29
#: ../../talk/call.rst:172
msgid "Controlling audio and video"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:31
msgid "Use the microphone and camera icons at the bottom of the video preview to mute or unmute your microphone and enable or disable your camera before joining."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:33
msgid "If one or both of your icons are greyed out, you either do not have a microphone or camera installed, or you did not give permission to the browser or Talk Desktop client to use your microphone or camera. Check that you have granted permission to the browser or Talk Desktop client, and make sure your microphone and camera are not in use by another application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:37
msgid "Device settings allow you to choose which microphone and camera you want to use. This is useful if you have more than one microphone or camera available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:39
msgid "Talk media settings showing microphone and camera device selection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:44
msgid "Noise suppression"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:46
msgid "Enable noise suppression to reduce background noise during calls with following steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:48
msgid "Open ``Media settings`` before or during a call"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:49
msgid "Locate the ``Microphone settings`` section"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:50
msgid "Enable ``Noise suppression`` at desired level"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:52
msgid "Auto-gain control and echo cancellation options are also available in the same section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:54
msgid "Talk media settings showing microphone options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:59
msgid "Backgrounds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:61
msgid "Backgrounds let you replace your video background with one of the predefined images. You can also upload your own image or choose one already in Nextcloud Files. Alternatively, choose the ``blur`` option to blur your live video background."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:65
msgid "Talk media settings showing virtual background and blur options for video"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:70
msgid "Immediately join a call"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:72
msgid "If you wish to skip ``Media settings`` in the future, toggle the ``Skip device preview before joining a call`` switch in app settings. For future calls in this conversation, you will join directly, skipping the preview dialog."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:76
msgid "Record a call"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:78
msgid "If you started the call and wish to record it, check the ``Start recording immediately with the call`` checkbox. The call recording option might not be available to you, depending on whether your system administrators have enabled this option and whether you have ``Moderator`` permission for the conversation. If you are joining and the call is being recorded, you might be required to consent before being allowed to join. For more information, see :ref:`Call recording <call-recording>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:85
msgid "Start the call"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:87
msgid "Click the ``Start call`` button at the bottom of ``Media settings`` to notify all conversation participants of the call. If you do not want to notify the other participants, start a silent call by opening the three-dot menu to the left of the ``Start call`` button and choosing ``Call without notification``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:91
msgid "Talk Call without notification option in media settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:95
msgid "Talk confirmation step for calling without sending a notification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:99
msgid "Other participants can modify notifications on a per-conversation level, including whether they want to receive call notifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:101
msgid "Your user status will be set to ``In a call`` and your user status icon will display the speech bubble emoji."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:104
msgid "Mobile clients"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:106
msgid "When you are part of a conversation and have permission to do so, you can start a call at any time by tapping the ``Phone`` or ``Video`` icon in the top bar. The ``Phone`` icon starts a voice-only call; the ``Video`` icon starts a video call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:110
msgid "A voice call uses the device microphone and earpiece, like a regular phone call. A video call uses the loudspeaker in hands-free mode and enables your front-facing camera by default; you can disable it at any time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:113
msgid "If someone else starts a call, you may receive a notification and your device may ring or vibrate, depending on your notification settings. Tap ``Phone`` or ``Video`` to join, or tap the red button to decline. Declining dismisses the call notification on that device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:117
msgid "You can control your microphone and camera (if in a video call) with the options shown at the bottom of the screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:119
msgid "Your user status will be set to ``In a call`` and your user status icon will display a speech bubble."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:122
msgid "During a call"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:124
msgid "After you join a call, you will see the call view. It shows the video feeds of all participants currently in the call, with additional information and controls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:126
msgid "Talk active call view showing participant video feeds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:130
msgid "The leftmost element shows the elapsed call time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:132
msgid "Next to it, you will see the number of participants that have joined the current call. Clicking the number opens the right sidebar and shows the list of participants. Participants that have joined the call will be listed first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:136
msgid "You will also see each participant's talking time if they have spoken during the call:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:138
msgid "Talk active call showing talking time indicator for each participant"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:142
msgid "You can access additional call options and settings from the three-dot menu in the top bar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:144
msgid "Talk in-call three-dot menu for additional settings and options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:149
msgid "Set up breakout rooms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:151
msgid "Breakout rooms allow you to divide a call into smaller groups for more focused discussions. Depending on your permissions and how your instance is configured, this option may not be available to you. For more information, see :ref:`Breakout rooms <breakout-rooms>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:156
msgid "Download call participants list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:158
msgid "You can download the list of participants in a call from the three-dot menu in the top bar. This downloads a CSV file with the names and email addresses of all participants."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:160
msgid "Talk in-call menu showing download participants list option"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:164
msgid "The CSV file contains the following columns:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:166
msgid "**Name**: The name of the participant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:167
msgid "**Email**: The email address of the participant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:168
msgid "**Type**: Indicates whether the participant is a registered user or a guest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:169
msgid "**Identifier**: Unique identifier for the participant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:174
msgid "Bottom bar of the call view offers media controls, layout settings and other features you can use during a call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:176
msgid "Talk active call bottom bar showing media controls and layout settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:180
msgid "Use the microphone and camera icons to mute/unmute your microphone and enable/disable your camera. You can also use the keyboard shortcuts :kbd:`M` to mute/unmute your microphone and :kbd:`V` to enable/disable your camera. Use :kbd:`Space` for push-to-talk: holding space temporarily unmutes you while muted, or temporarily mutes you while unmuted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:185
msgid "Reactions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:187
msgid "The reactions button lets you send an emoji reaction to all participants in the call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:189
msgid "Talk active call reactions panel with emoji options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:193
msgid "Every participant will see the emoji rising from the bottom of their call screen. The emoji disappears after two seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:196
msgid "Raise hand"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:198
msgid "Clicking ``Raise hand`` will notify moderators and show an icon next to your name. This is also available via the keyboard shortcut :kbd:`R`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:201
msgid "Full screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../talk/call.rst:203
msgid "Resizes your browser window or the Talk Desktop client to full-screen mode. Also available via the keyboard shortcut :kbd:`F`. Press :kbd:`Esc` to return to the regular view."
msgstr ""
